---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getLastUpdated, getLivePlans, getProviders } from '../lib/data';
import { formatDate } from '../lib/format';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, GITHUB_URL, SITE_NAME, SITE_URL } from '../lib/site';

const plans = getLivePlans();
const providers = getProviders();
const lastUpdated = getLastUpdated();

const structuredData = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'AboutPage',
  name: `About ${SITE_NAME}`,
  url: `${SITE_URL}/about/`,
  description: 'About VM Compare South Africa, an independent weekly comparison of VPS prices.',
  isPartOf: { '@type': 'WebSite', name: SITE_NAME, url: SITE_URL },
};
---

<Base
  title="About VM Compare South Africa"
  description="VM Compare is an independent weekly comparison of VPS and VM prices in South African data centres, built as a companion to number1.co.za."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
  jsonLd={structuredData}
>
  <section class="provider-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-label">About</span>
      <h1>About VM Compare</h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">
        A small, independent project that answers one question properly: what is the cheapest VM
        you can get in a South African data centre?
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>Why this exists</h2>
      <p>
        Shopping for a VPS in South Africa usually means opening a dozen provider sites, working out
        which prices include VAT, spotting that the headline price is a first-month promotion, and
        then comparing wildly different RAM, vCPU and storage combinations. That is tedious and easy
        to get wrong.
      </p>
      <p>
        VM Compare collects the public prices, normalises them to VAT-inclusive rand, ignores
        promotional teasers, and presents the result in one filterable table. It is a companion to
        the <a href="https://number1.co.za" rel="noopener">number1.co.za</a> articles on
        <a href="https://number1.co.za/cheapest-vps-linux-server-vm-in-south-africa/" rel="noopener">cheapest VPS hosting in South Africa</a>
        and
        <a href="https://number1.co.za/best-bang-for-buck-linux-vps-vm-in-south-africa-2026/" rel="noopener">best bang for buck VPS in 2026</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What is included</h2>
      <p>
        The current dataset has <strong>{plans.length} live plans</strong> from
        <strong>{providers.length} providers</strong>, last checked {formatDate(lastUpdated)}. We
        include providers with a real, orderable VPS product in a South African data centre.
        International providers with a Johannesburg region are listed separately rather than mixed
        into the local comparison.
      </p>

      <h2>Independence</h2>
      <p>
        No provider pays to be listed or ranked. The comparison is generated from public pricing
        pages and a small amount of manual verification. If affiliate links are added later, they
        will be disclosed and will not change the ordering.
      </p>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        Prices change, promotions end, and pages get redesigned. If you spot something wrong, email
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> with the provider, plan and a link,
        and it will be fixed. The data pipeline and site source are public on
        <a href={GITHUB_URL} rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Provider listing requests, corrections and general questions:
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
